    "result_text": "The suite consists of the single AcceptanceTest (plus base/helper classes), and it's green. The build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` derivation on the Owner resource so that `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns the IANA timezone name derived from the owner's locality/region.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `timezone` string property to the `Owner` schema (right after `locality`), documenting the fixed region\u2192timezone table. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with the field at build time.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 \n   - Added the `@Mapping(target = \"timezone\", ...)` binding on `toOwnerDto`.\n   - Added the fixed `REGION_TIMEZONE` table (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`).\n   - Added `toTimezone(Owner)`, which reuses the existing locality/region derivation (`toLocality`) and maps it through the table, returning `null` for regions not in the table.\n\nDeriving from `toLocality` keeps `timezone` consistent with the already-existing `locality` field (postcode-preferred, city fallback, `customerCode` prefix when present), so for the test's `knownOwner(\"Sydney\")` (postcode 2000 \u2192 NSW) it returns `Australia/Sydney`.\n\nThe full test suite (`AcceptanceTest`, which asserts `locality=NSW` and `timezone=Australia/Sydney`) passes: **BUILD SUCCESS**, Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0.",
